## BLOCKING B1 — validateOpusFront under-validates; a branch-committed record crashes the board client
Code: adapters/native/src/index.ts:368-385 (validateOpusFront). It checks id, state, gate status, tokens, traditio and title only. Its docstring says it
"accepts exactly what check accepts"; check (check.ts:495-498) requires opus.sella to be a declared string, so that claim is false.
Reproduced (probe6/7): sample-studio copy in a git repo, branch opus/W-002 whose COMMITTED record has `sella: { a: 1 }`.
  readCandidate accepts it (branchRecords status ok, dropped []), store.api.opera() serves sella as {"a":1}, and a React render of it throws
  "Objects are not valid as a React child". Board.tsx has no error boundary, so one builder-committed field blanks the Patron's board on every poll.
Class — every unvalidated record field that reaches a React child. Enumerated by grepping apps/web/src for `{...sella|collegium|evidence}` children:
  1. `sella`: BoardView.tsx:66 (Card, whole board) and BoardDrawer.tsx:26. Probe: object sella -> served as object -> throws.
  2. gate `evidence` (toOpus maps `{href: g.evidence}`): BoardDrawer.tsx:60, `{g.evidence}` as a child. Probe7: `evidence: { a: 1 }` -> served
     as {"href":{"a":1}} -> throws when that card's drawer opens.
  3. gate `certifies` (same shape, adapters/native/src/index.ts toOpus): not rendered today, but it is typed string and unchecked. Same fix.
  Checked and safe: title (validated string), traditio values (board.ts:352 filters to strings), collegium (template-literal use only),
  tokens (finite number), heartbeat (not rendered anywhere), body (plain text child).
Fix is one place: validateOpusFront rejects a non-string sella/collegium/kind and a non-string gate evidence/certifies (when present), so the record
  drops as `invalid-shape`. Optionally also coerce in board.ts cardRow. Add rows for sella, evidence and certifies as objects to the shape-validation behaviour.
Trunk records with the same defect were already a board crash (check blocks them); the new thing is that a branch tip is builder-controlled and unreviewed.

